        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Héctor Canziani, Oscar Wilde\n- Works: Al Compás de tu Mentira\n- Roles: film director, film producer, screenwriter, poet, writer\n- Topics: tango film, adapted plays\n\nFacts:\n- Oscar Wilde was an Irish writer who lived from 16 October 1854 to 30 November 1900 and wrote plays, fiction, essays, and poetry.\n- Héctor Canziani had a brief film career and later produced more work in screenwriting and poetry.\n- Héctor Canziani is best known for directing and producing the 1950 tango dancing film Al Compás de tu Mentira.\n- Al Compás de tu Mentira was based on a play by Oscar Wilde.",
